e their growing settlement  [Music]  valhalla's story plays out over a series  of self-contained narrative arcs  by talking to sigurd's wife ranvi evil  can choose which alliances to pursue  next which kicks off a two to three hour  story  upon completion evol returns to ranvi  and reports on what transpired invests  any collected resources into a  settlement and then picks the next  narrative thread once an arc is done  it's done certain characters can come  back in later arcs but that is  very rare to the game's benefit this  means that if a specific narrative arc  has characters or gameplay that you  don't necessarily enjoy  you know that once the arc is over  you're likely never going to have to  engage with that pocket of england ever  again the story will soon move past that  arc and then largely act like it never  existed giving you new characters to me  and mission structures to engage with  however this works against the game too  as anything you like  won't last either the biggest detriment  of the self-contained arcs is the  somewhat shallow supporting cast  because characters typically only stick  around for a few hours there isn't much  time for development  and where there is any it's rushed  romances especially suffer for this  they're shallow and don't have any  meaningful impact on eva or story  avail is the one that bugs the trend of  paper-thin characters in valhalla though  their actual character is already  established you get to push  and prod at their thoughts and actions  evolve wants to avoid their fate  and you get to influence how far they're  willing to go to ensure that outcome do  we have any allies to speak of  or is that your excuse to do nothing the  decisions you make determine how  others view evil which can result in  slight alterations to how certain arcs  and the campaign as a whole end there's  small changes that avoid outright  redefining the timeline of real human  history  instead focusing on giving you the room  to somewhat shape avor into your desired  protagonist  aval's lasting impact or the potential  for it is  also an effective driving force to carry  players through to the end  figuring out how a random viking from  the 800s will save the world in 2020  is an intriguing proposition especially  since valhalla does a good job of laying  breadcrumbs of knowledge and small  revelations throughout its run time to  keep you chasing the answer to that  question  overall this storytelling structure  works out for valhalla its pacing isn't  without its issues the opening hours are  a slog to get through for example  but once it hits his stride with  memorable arcs and more things to do in  the settlement valhalla starts to  exhibit the kind of confidence you'd  expect in the third goal at an  open world rpg style of assassin's creed  it just takes some time to get to that  point  valhalla trusts you to think like an  explorer to put yourself in a war's  shoes as they navigate and attempt to  understand  england this is still a ubisoft game  that's packed with waypoints to follow  for the main campaign and side missions  but in valhalla they're also designed to  encourage you towards discovery and the  game has such  wonderful heartbreaking hilarious and  intriguing things to look for off the  beaten path  excuse me i have a slight pain  do you notice anything on my head  in its combat you'll find the most  agency in how you shape able  earning skill points allows you to  invest in the constellation-like skill  tree the constellation of lines twist  and turn on one another allowing you to  easily double back  invest in more than one tree while also  having different branches of each tree  cross over for more interesting build  opportunities  you can respect aval skills at any time  for free allowing you to easily reshape  them if one combat style isn't to your  liking  regardless of where you put your skill  points avo is a badass raider who deal  wields weapons with a frenzied intensity  valhalla encourages you to fight  aggressively avail doesn't regenerate  health and your healing rations are  limited so it's in your best interest to  end fights as quickly as possible by  assassinating an opponent or disrupting  the tempo of their attacks with powerful  strikes counters or blocks button  mashing will deliver you to an early  grave strategically playing to your  strengths is the only way to succeed  against tougher foes  abilities are where valhalla's combat  gets exciting you can equip  8 at one time allowing you to further  define your ideal build for evil through  both skills and abilities and the way  the game gives you the adrenaline needed  to execute them you're encouraged to  begin fights with a quick  decisive strike and then aggressively  keep up the pressure to win  valhalla also sees you fight your enemy  with social stealth this is used to  great effect in some of the more tense  story arcs where evol  is hunting members of the order of  ancients in cities that the group or an  enemy king controls  forcing them to blend in and parkour  across rooftops until they can close in  on their target  however the parkour mechanics aren't as  good as those seen in some previous  entries so avo can feel a bit clunky  when trying to stealth  it's frustrating when you accidentally  die or get noticed because the controls  are working against you it occasionally  feels like it would have been easier  just to announce yourself  and kill everyone in the vicinity  instead and if you want to do that  that's fine valhalla does not  immediately fail you for being detected  although the assassin's creed franchise  will no doubt continue there is a real  sense of finality to valhalla's main  campaign  valhalla brings together dozens of  narrative threads referencing nearly  every mainline game in the franchise to  tell you how they all connect  in this way the game can feel  specifically designed for longtime fans  however  assassin's creed valhalla is more than  capable of standing on its own  aval is a good hero with an identity  that drives the mystery behind the main  narrative and they shine in the  self-contained arc structure of  valhalla's story the supporting cast may  not shine as brightly but it's easy to  forgive that when exploring england is  so rewarding  [Music]  foreign

